WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.000
It’s Professor Dave, let’s check out Legionnaires’ Disease.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:16.320
Legionnaires’ disease, also called Legionellosis,
is a severe, often lethal form of pneumonia,

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.360
which just means lung inflammation.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.650
Symptoms may include cough, muscle aches,
diarrhea, fever, and chills.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.591
In the U.S., somewhere between 10,000 and
18,000 people get infected each year, some

00:00:29.591 --> 00:00:32.660
of which end up in intensive care units.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:38.760
We first learned about this disease in 1976,
when a mysterious outbreak of pneumonia occurred

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.300
at an American Legion convention in Philadelphia,
hence the name.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.649
Because of the fatal nature of some of the
cases, health officials launched an intensive

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:53.890
investigation that resulted in the definition
of a new family of pathogenic bacteria, the

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.630
Legionellaceae.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:03.040
The family Legionellaceae consists of a single
genus, Legionella, with 48 species and 70

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.040
serogroups.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.750
These bacteria are slender gram-negative rods
that are pleomorphic, which means they can

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:14.900
change shape in response to their environment.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:20.980
Infection with Legionella pneumophila has
three possible outcomes: One is no symptoms at all.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.440
Two, an influenza-like illness called Pontiac
fever.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.850
And three, legionnaires’ disease, a severe
form of pneumonia.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:37.240
Legionella is naturally found in freshwater
lakes and streams, but can be particularly

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.350
dangerous to humans when it spreads in man-made
building water systems like cooling towers,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.590
plumbing systems, hot water heaters, or decorative
fountains.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:53.240
In particular, these bacteria thrive in the
mist created by air-conditioning ducts, and

00:01:53.240 --> 00:02:00.189
can infect an entire building of people, like
that fateful summer of 1976 in Philadelphia.

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:06.409
A person becomes infected by breathing in
small droplets of water that contain Legionella,

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:09.509
and typically can’t spread the disease to
other people.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:15.090
Legionnaires’ disease most often develops
in people with an already increased likelihood

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.860
of developing respiratory sickness, such as
those who smoke cigarettes or those with a

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.760
compromised immune system.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:28.120
The Legionella, if able to establish an infection,
replicate within cells of the immune system.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:35.040
After an incubation period of two to ten days,
an infection of L. pneumophila can cause acute

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.950
illness, which can escalate to multi-organ
disease of the gastrointestinal tract, liver,

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.430
central nervous system, or the kidneys.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:51.090
To diagnose a case of Legionnaires’ disease,
clinicians typically take a chest x-ray, and

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:56.530
might conduct a urine test or saliva test
to confirm the presence of the bacteria.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:02.040
Typically, antibiotics can clear an infection
of legionnaires’ disease, but approximately

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.570
10% of people who get sick with the disease
will die due to complications.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:13.160
The best way to prevent Legionnaires’ disease
is to properly maintain building water systems,

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.850
hot tubs, and fountains.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:20.420
So if you have many hot tubs and fountains
in your mansion, be sure to take precautions now.

